This file is a placeholder indicating that the embedded unity-plugin-library.jar should not be used by the Android build.

Reason:
- The project now uses Gradle-managed Google Play services (com.google.android.gms:play-services-ads). The embedded JAR `unity-plugin-library.jar` contains classes that duplicate those provided by the Gradle dependency and can cause "Duplicate class" errors during Gradle build (APK/AAR packaging).

Action taken by maintainer/assistant:
- Assets/Plugins/Android/mainTemplate.gradle has been updated to exclude `unity-plugin-library.jar` from the libs fileTree so it's not packaged by Gradle.

Recommended final step (safe removal):
- Remove the actual JAR from the repository to avoid any accidental usage in other parts of the pipeline:
  git rm Assets/Plugins/Android/GoogleMobileAdsPlugin/libs/unity-plugin-library.jar
  git commit -m "Remove embedded unity-plugin-library.jar to avoid duplicate classes with Gradle play-services-ads"

If you prefer not to remove the file, you can keep this placeholder and rename the JAR locally (or on a branch) to `unity-plugin-library.jar.disabled` instead.
